# Duck Embody — environment configuration TEMPLATE
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your keys:
#     cp .env.example .env && ${EDITOR:-nano} .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored and must NEVER be committed (AGENTS.md hard rule 6:
# secrets come from the environment only, never from a tracked file).
# Load it before running anything that calls a model API:
#     set -a && source .env && set +a
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED — model provider keys
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Anthropic — drives the Fable 5 and Opus 5 benchmark cells, and the VLM
# room-recognition gate in T2.3 (scene survey).
# Get one at: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# OpenAI — drives the GPT 5.6 sol benchmark cell.
# Get one at: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# Optional in a pinch: if this key is absent the runner can still execute the
# two Anthropic cells (see the cut order in docs/PLAN.md).
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — overrides (leave unset to use the defaults in configs/)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Parent robot project checkout (supplies the Isaac Lab task registration that
# duck_embody/env/embody_env_cfg.py imports). Default: ~/Projects/Open_Duck_Mini_Jetson
# DUCK_EMBODY_PARENT_REPO=/home/you/Projects/Open_Duck_Mini_Jetson

# Isaac Lab checkout (used to locate isaaclab.sh for kit-python runs).
# Default: ~/IsaacLab
# ISAACLAB_PATH=/home/you/IsaacLab

# Where trial JSONs, videos and figures are written. Default: ./results
# DUCK_EMBODY_RESULTS_DIR=/path/to/results

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COST WARNING
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A full benchmark batch is 12 trials (3 models x 4 seeds), each up to ~80 model
# turns with images. Estimated spend is documented in
# docs/designs/06-benchmark-evaluation.html section 8. Check your provider
# spend limits before launching the batch (docs/PLAN.md T4.3).
